        "mark_scheme_text": "2(a) horizontal force on sphere causes centripetal acceleration B1\nweight of sphere is (now) equal to vertical component of tension B1\nor\nhorizontal and vertical components (of force) (now) combine to give greater tension (in spring)\ngreater tension in spring so greater extension of spring B1\n\n2(b)(i) r = 10.8  sin 27° = 4.9 cm A1\n\n2(b)(ii) T cos  = mg C1\nor\nT cos  = W and W = mg\nT cos 27° = 0.29  9.81 leading to T = 3.2 N A1\n\n2(b)(iii) T = 3.2 – (0.29  9.81) C1\nk = T / x A1\n= [3.2 – (0.29  9.81)] / [10.8 – 8.5]\n= 0.15 N cm–1\n\n2(c)(i) centripetal acceleration = (T sin ) / m C1\n= (3.2  sin 27°) / 0.29\n= 5.0 m s–2 A1\n© UCLES 2023 Page 7 of 16\n\n2(c)(ii) a = r2 and  = 2 / T C1\nor\na = v2 / r and v = 2r / T\nT = 2  √(0.049 / 5.0) A1\n= 0.62 s\n© UCLES 2023 Page 8 of 16"
      }
