        "mark_scheme_text": "1(a) angle (subtended at centre of circle) when arc length = radius B1\n\n1(b)  = 2 / T C1\n= 2 / (1.0  60  60) A1\n= 1.7  10–3 rad s–1\n\n1(c)(i) angle = 1.7  10–3  1400 A1\n= 2.4 rad\n\n1(c)(ii) L = arc length / angle C1\n= 0.44 / 2.4\nor\nL = 0.44  (3600 / 1400) / 2\nL = 0.18 m A1\n\n1(c)(iii) a = r2 C1\n= 0.18  (1.745  10–3)2 A1\n= 5.5  10–7 m s–2\n\n1(d) centripetal acceleration is negligible compared with acceleration of free fall B1\nor\nnumerical comparison establishing answer to (c)(iii) ≪ 9.81\nresultant force is negligible compared with weight (of modelling clay) (so variation is negligible) B1\nor\nforce exerted by minute hand (approximately) equal (and opposite) to weight of modelling clay\n© UCLES 2023 Page 6 of 15"
